# Line endings are LF in the repository *and* in the working tree, on every
# platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true checks every text file out as CRLF on
# Windows; the mixed-line-ending pre-commit hook rewrites it back to LF and
# fails the commit over a change git itself considers empty. Retrying loops,
# because pre-commit restores the staged files with `git checkout`, which
# re-applies the CRLF. An eol attribute takes precedence over core.autocrlf,
# which is what ends it.
#
# All 56 tracked blobs were already LF in the index when this was added, so it
# changes what lands in the working tree, never what is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries stay byte-for-byte. The weights, the index and the source PDF are
# gitignored, so these rules are a guard against a stray copy being committed
# and silently corrupted by line-ending translation, not a description of the
# current tree.
*.pdf binary
*.safetensors binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.faiss binary
*.onnx binary
